1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,456
Day two. The Department of Unfortunate Outcomes no longer officially existed. This was the day humanity chose to be contacted.

2
00:00:08,836 --> 00:00:11,384
Gary. We are receiving a transmission.

3
00:00:11,664 --> 00:00:13,437
Not now.

4
00:00:13,717 --> 00:00:15,890
It originates outside the solar system.

5
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:18,512
Still not now.

6
00:00:19,892 --> 00:00:22,457
It is addressed to the highest authority on Earth.

7
00:00:22,737 --> 00:00:25,056
Then why is it ringing here?

8
00:00:25,336 --> 00:00:29,815
A typo. Our postal code is one digit away from the United Nations.

9
00:00:30,095 --> 00:00:32,252
Of course it is.

10
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:38,752
Gary! There's an alien in the lobby! He's so tall! He brought a gift!

11
00:00:39,032 --> 00:00:41,078
Is he on the visitor list?

12
00:00:41,358 --> 00:00:42,157
I'll check!

13
00:00:43,537 --> 00:00:46,169
Name, species, reason for visit?

14
00:00:46,449 --> 00:00:50,650
Ambassador Ixx. Vael. First contact.

15
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:54,501
There are only ten boxes for the name.

16
00:00:54,781 --> 00:00:56,858
Then I shall be Ixx of Vael.

17
00:00:58,238 --> 00:01:04,749
People of Earth. Eleven days ago we detected a singularity in your accounting department.

18
00:01:05,029 --> 00:01:06,193
That was ours.

19
00:01:06,473 --> 00:01:11,764
It vanished. My civilization required four thousand years to achieve that.

20
00:01:12,044 --> 00:01:13,737
We fed it paperwork.

21
00:01:14,017 --> 00:01:15,892
...Teach us.

22
00:01:17,272 --> 00:01:21,783
Your species has weaponized bureaucracy. We bow before you.

23
00:01:22,063 --> 00:01:23,348
Technically correct.

24
00:01:23,628 --> 00:01:27,284
It's not a weapon. It's a Tuesday.

25
00:01:28,664 --> 00:01:37,251
Unfortunately, protocol requires your formal reply within one Earth day. Otherwise your planet is declared unclaimed and reassigned.

26
00:01:37,531 --> 00:01:39,549
Reassigned to whom?

27
00:01:39,829 --> 00:01:41,074
A mining company.

28
00:01:41,354 --> 00:01:44,336
What do we have to file?

29
00:01:44,616 --> 00:01:48,210
Form 7-J. Fourteen pages. Notarized.

30
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:51,809
Notarized by whom?

31
00:01:52,089 --> 00:01:53,488
A neutral party.

32
00:01:53,768 --> 00:01:54,958
Dave is a notary.

33
00:01:55,238 --> 00:01:57,331
Dave is in Portugal.

34
00:01:57,611 --> 00:02:00,266
I'll ask Dave! Does he have Wi-Fi?

35
00:02:01,646 --> 00:02:03,589
Out of toner.

36
00:02:03,869 --> 00:02:05,225
We have eleven minutes.

37
00:02:05,505 --> 00:02:06,942
Nobody panic.

38
00:02:07,222 --> 00:02:09,822
Eleven minutes!

39
00:02:11,202 --> 00:02:20,589
Thank you for calling Toner Express. Your order is important to us. Estimated delivery: six to eight weeks. Press one to hear this message again.

40
00:02:21,969 --> 00:02:24,750
Form rejected. Signed by an intern.

41
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:27,498
I'm the only one here.

42
00:02:27,778 --> 00:02:33,412
Gary. A legally non-existent entity cannot be rejected. It can only be pending.

43
00:02:33,692 --> 00:02:37,829
...Pending is acceptable. Review time: six hundred years.

44
00:02:39,209 --> 00:02:50,053
Earth was not destroyed. It was placed on hold. Estimated wait time: six hundred years. Gary's mood: unchanged. Next time on Department of Unfortunate Outcomes: Dolores Files a Complaint.
